  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Why a hook needs all five layers",
      "items": [
        "Nothing in JavaScript can read a thermal sensor; the value has to cross into native code",
        "Expo Modules is where PixelKit's Kotlin lives, which is why a development build is required and Expo Go can never work",
        "The HAL is the boundary where a reading either exists or does not, which is what source: 'unavailable' reports"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "What crosses, and how often",
      "items": [
        "Hooks poll on an interval you set rather than streaming, so the bridge is not the bottleneck",
        "Readings cross as plain numbers, not objects, so there is no serialisation cost worth tuning",
        "A hook that cannot reach its layer returns null instead of retrying, so a missing HAL never blocks a render"
      ]
    }
  ]
